# =============================================================================
# The Governance Framework — protective .gitignore defaults
# =============================================================================
#
# These defaults assume your project repository may become public or be
# accessed by people outside your team. TGF artifacts contain operational
# security information valuable to attackers if exposed.
#
# Override consciously: uncomment or remove lines below if you want artifact
# transparency for team-shared or open-source projects.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Always gitignored — contains working decisions, exploration, and ephemeral
# operational data.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.sessions/
.tgf/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operational security artifacts — gitignored by default. Public exposure
# helps attackers reconnaissance the project.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md
docs/DOMAIN-CONTEXT.md
docs/THREAT-MODEL.md
docs/BASELINE-AUDIT.md
docs/ERROR-LOG.md
docs/VENDOR-LOG.md
docs/WAIVER-LOG.md
docs/audits/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decision and roadmap artifacts — gitignored by default for solo projects.
# Consider committing for team transparency by commenting out the three lines
# below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/DECISIONS.md
docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/SCHEMA-HISTORY.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Framework adoption indicators
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md and .claude/skills/ ARE typically committed so the framework
# travels with the codebase. Uncomment below ONLY if you want to hide TGF
# adoption entirely (e.g., for projects where revealing the framework's
# presence is itself a security concern):
#
# CLAUDE.md
# .claude/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standard ignores (keep these regardless of TGF policy)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
